    exportControl 	"Public"
    logical_models 	(list unit_reference_list
	(object UseCase "Modify Boundary"
	    quid       	"3A1E2528031A"
	    documentation 	
|The user modifies the boundary by changing a rectangle in the top view.The user can change the orientation of the model (rotate on z-axis). All geometry views are shown with respect to the (new) orientation of the boundary.
|
|In some cases (for example if a model contains faults) modifying the boundary can change the number of bodys or the definition of the bodies and therfore invalidate (remove) the bodys assigned to the formations (Autodetect-Bodies must be invoked to recalculate the definition of the bodies)
|
|Modifying the boundary causes restoring the initial mesh for all
|horizons and faults. All Defined mesh regions are relative to the boundary and therfore stay intact.
|
|
	    )
	(object UseCase "Best Fit"
	    quid       	"3A23719A0269"
	    documentation 	
|If information of reservoirs is known then adjust the size of the boundary to the reservoir-size else adjust the size according the geometry of the model. The rectangular size can only changed in the topview (x,y plane) and rotated on the z axis.
|
|
|
|
|
	    )
